+upgrade permission. The original binding/producer/gate boundaries still apply.
+
+Consumer qualification subsequently confirmed the missing native directory
+custody. The selected producer and native adapter now refuse before their first
+effect; the service reports `ORIGINAL_NATIVE_DIRECTORY_CUSTODY_REQUIRED` on HOLD.
+The exact required kernel-handle interface and the swap-after-last-observation
+regression are documented in
+[Recovery directory custody required](RECOVERY_DIRECTORY_CUSTODY_REQUIRED.md).
+
+The selector's own registration/create effects are also withheld. Without
+original parent-namespace custody, absent registration now gives
+`owned_protected_backup_root_original_parent_namespace_custody_required` before
+REGISTERING or mkdir. Actual selector scopes are read-only (`registration:null`);
+existing READY observations do not discharge the unchanged recovery-effect veto.
